SESSION 2: AUTHENTICATION BUGS AND SUPABASE INTEGRATION
================================================================================

[ISSUES FIXED]
1. User login/signup info not being stored
2. Add to cart not working
3. Google authentication not working

Root Causes Identified:
- Supabase credentials were hardcoded as placeholders ('YOUR_SUPABASE_URL')
- Missing imports in userManager.js (supabase, getCurrentUser)
- Duplicate imports causing module errors
- Google OAuth redirect using absolute path /index.html instead of relative

Changes Made:
- Fixed userManager.js: Removed duplicate imports, added missing ones
- Fixed source/auth.js: Changed Google OAuth redirect from "/index.html" to window.location.origin
- Created SUPABASE_SETUP.md with comprehensive setup guide

Files Modified:
  ✓ source/userManager.js
  ✓ source/auth.js
  
Files Created:
  ✓ SUPABASE_SETUP.md (Setup guide with SQL queries)

Database Setup Required:
  - user_profiles table
  - carts table
  - wishlist table
  - orders table
  - order_items table
  - Row Level Security (RLS) policies

================================================================================
SESSION 3: AUTHENTICATION STATE AND CART BUTTON ISSUES
================================================================================

[ISSUES FIXED]
1. Login status of user unknown after page load
2. Cart button showing signup popup even after logging in
3. Cart count not updating in real-time

Root Cause: 
- Page load event fired before Supabase restored session from Google OAuth redirect
- Using getCurrentUser() was too slow, session not yet restored

Solution Implemented:
- Added supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange() listener for real-time auth detection
- Works for all login methods (email, Google, etc.)
- Automatically detects when session is restored from localStorage

Changes Made:
- Updated index.html: Replaced auth detection logic with onAuthStateChange listener
- Added updateUIForLoggedInUser() and updateUIForLoggedOutUser() functions
- Cart button now shows ONLY when authenticated
- Updated script.js: Cart button now navigates to cart.html instead of showing popup
- Added console logging for debugging auth state

Files Modified:
  ✓ index.html
  ✓ script.js

Result:
  ✓ User login status now detected immediately
  ✓ Cart button hidden until login, visible after login
  ✓ No more signup popup for authenticated users
  ✓ Real-time UI updates on auth changes

